.TH XIL\-SFX\-MATCH "1" "2026\-08\-09" "xil\-pipeline 0.3.2" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
xil\-sfx\-match
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B xil\-sfx\-match
[-h] [--show SHOW] [--episode EPISODE] [--top TOP] [--min-coverage MIN_COVERAGE] [--output OUTPUT] [--emit-hints [PATH]] [--apply] [--accept-review] [--dry-run] [--quiet]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Find existing SFX library assets for cues whose declared source is not on disk — the cues that make 'xil produce' refuse to start. Reports by default; \-\-apply copies the match into the show's pool and journals the new source.

.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-show\fR \fI\,SHOW\/\fR
Restrict to one show slug (default: every show in the workspace)

.TP
\fB\-\-episode\fR \fI\,EPISODE\/\fR, \fB\-\-tag\fR \fI\,EPISODE\/\fR
Restrict to one episode tag (e.g. S01E01)

.TP
\fB\-\-top\fR \fI\,TOP\/\fR
Candidates to report per cue (default: 3)

.TP
\fB\-\-min\-coverage\fR \fI\,MIN_COVERAGE\/\fR
Coverage a candidate must reach to be reported (default: 0.5)

.TP
\fB\-\-output\fR \fI\,OUTPUT\/\fR
CSV output path, or '\-' for stdout (default: reports/sfx_match_<date>.csv)

.TP
\fB\-\-emit\-hints\fR \fI\,[PATH]\/\fR
Also write a paste\-ready pipe\-hint block (default path:
reports/sfx_match_hints_<date>.md)

.TP
\fB\-\-apply\fR
Copy each accepted match into the show's SFX pool under the cue's own slug,
retitle the copy, and journal the new source. Acts on EXACT and STRONG only
unless \-\-accept\-review is given.

.TP
\fB\-\-accept\-review\fR
Widen \-\-apply to REVIEW matches. Read the CSV first — a REVIEW tier means the
top candidate had no clear margin over its runners\-up.

.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
With \-\-apply, report every copy and journal record without writing

.TP
\fB\-\-quiet\fR
Suppress the console summary (CSV only)

